When the user's message names the files to deliver, present exactly those — no others and none missing. Otherwise the deliverables are the finished work this turn produced: documents, spreadsheets, slides, PDFs, images, audio or video, HTML or Markdown pages, archives. Do not present helper scripts, intermediate data or scratch files (they belong in the project's .work/ folder) unless the user explicitly asked for them, or anything you have not finished. Call it once, after the files are final, listing every deliverable; each one gets a download and preview card. Paths must be inside the project directory — save or copy a deliverable there first if it was written elsewhere. Presenting the same path again later records a new version.
